    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 220\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bills:\n \nSenate Bill Number 3951, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the state finance law, in relation to establishing\n      the civic education fund\"\n \nSenate Bill Number 4699, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT in relation to  requiring  the  commissioner  of  health  to\n      conduct a study relating to the number of emergency room beds\"\n \nSenate Bill Number 5202-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT directing a study on the impact of increased minimum wage on\n      eligibility for income-based services, programs and subsidies\"\n \nSenate Bill Number 5690, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend the New York state urban development corporation\n      act, in relation to evaluation and assistance to  increase  access\n      to child care\"\n \nSenate Bill Number 5716, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the urban development corporation act, in relation\n      to the beginning farmers NY fund\"\n \nSenate Bill Number 5855, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to direct the department of environmental conservation, with\n      the assistance of the department of transportation, to  conduct  a\n      study  on  the  environmental  and human health impacts of John F.\n      Kennedy international airport and LaGuardia airport\"\n \nSenate Bill Number 6553, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT establishing the New York task force on agricultural invest-\n      ment; and providing for the repeal of  such  provisions  upon  the\n      expiration thereof\"\n \nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bills:\n \nAssembly Bill Number 580, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the social services law, in relation to implement-\n      ing a cost estimation model for child care\"\n \nAssembly Bill Number 7574, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to exempting certain  car-\n      sharing organizations from the special supplemental tax on passen-\n \n      ger  car  rentals outside of the metropolitan commuter transporta-\ntion district\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  Each  of  these  bills would require significant state funding outside\nthe budget process. These bills require numerous  studies,  disbursement\nof  grants  with  no  funding  identified,  costly  tax  incentives, and\ncreation of new state offices and task forces.\n \n  The Legislature has failed, in every instance, to  identify  funds  to\nimplement  these  bills.  Programs  such as these, that have significant\nfiscal implications, must be discussed in  the  context  of  the  budget\nprocess.  It  is  irresponsible to have an agreement on a fiscal plan in\nApril, only to then pass these measures and provide no source  of  fund-\ning, leaving taxpayers on the hook and shortchanging existing programs.\n \n  While each of these proposals have merit and are laudable in their own\nright,  these decisions are appropriately made in the budget when global\nbudget discussions and  negotiations  occur.  For  these  insurmountable\nfiscal  reasons, I am vetoing these bills, although I welcome the oppor-\ntunity to discuss these studies, grant funds, tax incentives, and  state\noffices and task forces in the context of the budget.\n \n  These bills are disapproved.                (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
